# README criterion 9/AC9 (agent-exchange-2026-08 P12 G4): "No field
# classified as tool-established can be set by an agent, asserted by a gate
# reading a declared fill-class table." schemas/fill-classes.yaml classifies
# `migrated_from` TOOL on envelope/v1/base ("minted or stamped, never
# typed") — the exact field a post-phase audit found typeable onto a v2
# contract draft before internal/template.schemaAllowsField's fill-class
# check landed (template.go's own doc comment). This is the CLI half of
# "both surfaces refuse" driven against the built binary — the audit found
# no txtar/e2e scenario had ever exec'd this refusal at the transport
# boundary. The MCP half shares the identical internal/template code path
# (internal/mcp/tools_new.go calls the same schemaAllowsField), but
# internal/e2e structurally never imports internal/mcp (this package's own
# doc comment: "parity is P14, blocked_by: [P10]") and internal/mcp/cmd/a2a
# sit off this wave's allowlist — so the MCP half stays recorded, not
# raised here; see this wave's report and the README's own AC9 line.
! exec a2a new question --field migrated_from=x
stderr 'migrated_from'

# --- MCP half (agent-exchange-2026-08 spec 04 AC 1, D4): a misspelled
# field on a GROUPED tool's own published action is refused, BY NAME,
# before any write is attempted — the defect this phase's own goal names
# ("an agent reads a2a_exchange's own published schema, sends refs, and
# gets success with the reference silently discarded"). Unlike the CLI
# scenario above (a fill-class refusal on a KNOWN field), this is the
# OTHER half spec 04 closes: an UNKNOWN field, on the wire, now refused at
# decode rather than silently dropped.
#
# tools_dispatch.go's newDispatch forwards a tools/call request's FULL raw
# arguments (discriminator included) to the matching per-action handler
# unchanged; that handler now decodes through decodeStrict (tools.go),
# which turns on encoding/json's DisallowUnknownFields. "idss" (a typo for
# the real "ids" field, LifecycleInput's own json tag) has no home on that
# struct, so the decode refuses it — before actor resolution, before any
# mirror read, before the write funnel, and so well before this tier's own
# A2A_GITHUB_API 403-only denial stub could ever fire (this scenario never
# reaches a host call at all: the refusal is a decode-time one).
#
# `a2a mcp` reads exactly ONE JSON-RPC request from stdin (stdin below) and
# exits cleanly once stdin hits EOF (internal/mcp/server.go's Serve) —
# regardless of whether the tools/call inside it succeeded or refused, so
# this is a bare `exec`, not `! exec`. A handler error is never a JSON-RPC
# PROTOCOL error (server.go's own contract): it is a well-formed
# `tools/call` RESULT with `"isError":true` and the error text in its own
# content block, so the assertion reads stdout's own JSON-RPC response
# line, not the process exit code.
stdin mcp_unknown_field.json
exec a2a mcp
stdout '"isError":true'
stdout 'unknown field'
stdout 'idss'

-- mcp_unknown_field.json --
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"a2a_lifecycle","arguments":{"action":"ack","idss":["XQ-axon-20260101-aaaa"]}}}
